<section class="mb-80">
<div class="md-w-75">
<h2 class="fs-24 lh-24 mb-24">Give shared content a clear home.</h2>
<p>Category records keep names, URLs, collection names, introductions and landing-page metadata together. The listing, sidebar and breadcrumb templates read that shared data, so a category does not need a separate rendering branch in each template.</p>
<p>The blog layout places a flexible post list beside a fixed-width category sidebar on wider screens. On smaller screens the sidebar follows the posts. The introduction sits above both columns, giving the page a clear starting point.</p>
<p>Shared templates support consistent changes as more content is added. Review the generated pages after an edit, including headings, navigation and metadata. Performance and accessibility still need checks with the content, images and settings used by the finished site.</p>
</div>
</section>
